IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- THE FIRST, SECOND AND THIRD SCHEDULES (part roc12, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
-- The "revoked Rules" are the Rules of Court (R 5); they are not among the sources.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` unless its GIVETH says otherwise.
--   JUST TRUE    the thing holds as the Schedule states it.
--   JUST FALSE   the Schedule says no in its own words (an "unless" or "if" condition not met).
--   NOTHING      the Schedule does not answer: it is silent, its wording limits the scope, or the answer lives in a
--                written law or a Schedule table that is not among the sources.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.


-- ===========================================================================
§ `First Schedule -- Saving and transitional provisions`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:7748 | 1. Despite Order 1, Rule 2(1), unless the Court otherwise directs and subject to any written law, the Rules of Court (R 5) (called the revoked Rules) as in force immediately before 1 April 2022 (called the relevant date) continue to apply to and in relation to — ( a )
@ref Sch 1 para 1 “relevant date” (src:7748)
`sch 1 para 1 the relevant date` MEANS Date 1 4 2022

DECLARE `sch 1 para 1 kind of proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order`
    `sch 1 para 1(b) the subsequent proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court pursuant to a transfer order`
    `sch 1 para 1(c) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in a District Court or a Magistrate's Court`
    `sch 1 para 1(c)(i) an application to the General Division to transfer proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court to the General Division, and the subsequent proceedings there`
    `sch 1 para 1(c)(ii) an appeal to the General Division from proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court`
    `sch 1 para 1(d) an appeal or originating summons filed in the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division`
    `sch 1 para 1 other proceedings`

-- src:7748 | 1. Despite Order 1, Rule 2(1), unless the Court otherwise directs and subject to any written law, the Rules of Court (R 5) (called the revoked Rules) as in force immediately before 1 April 2022 (called the relevant date) continue to apply to and in relation to — ( a )
-- src:7749 | any proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court) before the relevant date, until the disposal of those proceedings by the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including any application to the General Division for an order transferring those proceedings to a District Court or a Magistrate’s Court (called in this paragraph a transfer order);
-- src:7750 | ( b )
-- src:7751 | the subsequent proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate’s Court (as the case may be) pursuant to a transfer order;
-- src:7752 | ( c )
-- src:7753 | any proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in a District Court or a Magistrate’s Court before the relevant date, including — (i)
-- src:7754 | any application to the General Division for an order transferring those proceedings to the General Division, and the subsequent proceedings in the General Division if the proceedings are ordered to be transferred to the General Division; and
-- src:7755 | (ii)
-- src:7756 | any appeal to the General Division from those proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate’s Court; and
-- src:7757 | ( d )
-- src:7758 | any appeal or originating summons before the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division that was filed in the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division before the relevant date. [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
@ref Sch 1 para 1 (src:7748-7758)
GIVEN kind IS A `sch 1 para 1 kind of proceedings`
      `the date the proceedings were commenced, or the appeal or originating summons was filed` IS A DATE
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings have been disposed of by the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `sch 1 para 1 other proceedings`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names only proceedings of kinds (a) to (d)
    ELSE IF (kind EQUALS `sch 1 para 1(b) the subsequent proceedings in the District Court or Magistrate's Court pursuant to a transfer order`) OR `the date the proceedings were commenced, or the appeal or originating summons was filed` LESS THAN `sch 1 para 1 the relevant date`
         THEN IF (kind EQUALS `sch 1 para 1(a) proceedings commenced by writ of summons or originating summons in the General Division (including the Singapore International Commercial Court), including an application for a transfer order`) AND `the proceedings have been disposed of by the General Division`
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the disposal of those proceedings by the General Division" (the period ends at disposal)
              ELSE IF `the Court otherwise directs`
                   THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise directs"
                   ELSE IF `a written law provides otherwise`
                        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subject to any written law"; the written law is not among the sources
                        ELSE JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "commenced ... before the relevant date" and "filed ... before the relevant date"; proceedings commenced, or an appeal or originating summons filed, on or after the relevant date are outside the period the text fixes

-- src:7759 | 2. Despite Order 1, Rule 2(1), the revoked Rules as in force immediately before the relevant date continue to apply to and in relation to any proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal before the Court of Appeal or Appellate Division under these Rules, if the judgment or order of the lower Court appealed against was given or made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules (whether pursuant to this Schedule or otherwise).
@ref Sch 1 para 2 (src:7759)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal before the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judgment or order of the lower Court appealed against was given or made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules, whether pursuant to this Schedule or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 2 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings in the lower Court` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the proceedings are proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal before the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division under these Rules`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal before the Court of Appeal or Appellate Division under these Rules"
    ELSE IF `the judgment or order of the lower Court appealed against was given or made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules, whether pursuant to this Schedule or otherwise`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the judgment or order of the lower Court appealed against was given or made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules"

-- src:7760 | 3. A caveat against arrest that is entered in the record of caveats under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules and is in force immediately before the relevant date is deemed to be a caveat against arrest issued under Order 33, Rule 5 of these Rules, and the date of expiry of the caveat is the date on which the caveat would have expired but for the revocation of the revoked Rules.
@ref Sch 1 para 3 (src:7760)
GIVEN `the caveat against arrest was entered in the record of caveats under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the caveat is in force immediately before the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 1 para 3 the caveat is deemed to be a caveat against arrest issued under Order 33, Rule 5` MEANS
    IF `the caveat against arrest was entered in the record of caveats under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules` AND `the caveat is in force immediately before the relevant date`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A caveat against arrest that is entered in the record of caveats under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules and is in force immediately before the relevant date"

@ref Sch 1 para 3 (src:7760)
GIVEN `the date the caveat would have expired but for the revocation of the revoked Rules` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`sch 1 para 3 the date of expiry of the caveat` MEANS `the date the caveat would have expired but for the revocation of the revoked Rules`

