-- src:7763 | Application or disapplication of provisions to categories of cases
@ref Sch 2 (src:7761-7763)
-- The parameter is kept, and never read, so that the function has the type the lead wires to O 1 r 2(13)'s `second schedule the case is in a category it sets out` (PLAN section 5.2: MAYBE BOOLEAN in, MAYBE BOOLEAN out).
GIVEN `the case is in a category the Second Schedule sets out` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 the case is in a category it sets out` MEANS
    NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Second Schedule is a heading only in this text, so no category is stated; the asker's own answer, if there is one, is not used because the text gives nothing to compare it with

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Third Schedule -- Civil procedure conventions`
-- ===========================================================================


DECLARE `sch 3 convention` IS ONE OF
    `sch 3 item 1 the convention between the United Kingdom and Austria`
    `sch 3 item 2 the convention between the United Kingdom and Italy`
    `sch 3 item 3 the convention between the United Kingdom and Germany`
    `sch 3 item 4 the treaty between Singapore and the People's Republic of China`
    `sch 3 item 5 the Hague Service Convention of 15 November 1965`
    `sch 3 another instrument`

-- src:7769 | 1.
-- src:7770 | Convention between the United Kingdom and Austria regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters
-- src:7771 | T 2/1999
-- src:7772 | 2.
-- src:7773 | Convention between the United Kingdom and Italy regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters
-- src:7774 | T 3/1999
-- src:7775 | 3.
-- src:7776 | Convention between the United Kingdom and Germany regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters
-- src:7777 | T 4/1999
-- src:7778 | 4.
-- src:7779 | Treaty on Judicial Assistance in civil and commercial matters between the Republic of Singapore and the People’s Republic of China
-- src:7780 | T 2/2001
-- src:7781 | 5.
-- src:7782 | Convention on the Service Abroad of Judicial and Extrajudicial Documents in Civil or Commercial Matters done at The Hague on 15 November 1965
-- src:7783 | T 1/2023
@ref Sch 3 (src:7769-7783)
GIVEN convention IS A `sch 3 convention`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`sch 3 the title of the convention` MEANS
    CONSIDER convention
    WHEN `sch 3 item 1 the convention between the United Kingdom and Austria` THEN JUST "Convention between the United Kingdom and Austria regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters"
    WHEN `sch 3 item 2 the convention between the United Kingdom and Italy` THEN JUST "Convention between the United Kingdom and Italy regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters"
    WHEN `sch 3 item 3 the convention between the United Kingdom and Germany` THEN JUST "Convention between the United Kingdom and Germany regarding legal proceedings in civil and commercial matters"
    WHEN `sch 3 item 4 the treaty between Singapore and the People's Republic of China` THEN JUST "Treaty on Judicial Assistance in civil and commercial matters between the Republic of Singapore and the People’s Republic of China"
    WHEN `sch 3 item 5 the Hague Service Convention of 15 November 1965` THEN JUST "Convention on the Service Abroad of Judicial and Extrajudicial Documents in Civil or Commercial Matters done at The Hague on 15 November 1965"
    WHEN `sch 3 another instrument` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Third Schedule lists five instruments; any other instrument has no entry

