@ref Sch 3 (src:7769-7783)
GIVEN convention IS A `sch 3 convention`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER convention
    WHEN `sch 3 item 1 the convention between the United Kingdom and Austria` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3 item 2 the convention between the United Kingdom and Italy` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3 item 3 the convention between the United Kingdom and Germany` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3 item 4 the treaty between Singapore and the People's Republic of China` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3 item 5 the Hague Service Convention of 15 November 1965` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 3 another instrument` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the Third Schedule is a complete table of five conventions, so an instrument not among them is not set out in it; whether it is a Civil Procedure Convention is O 1 r 3(1)'s "includes" limb (the keel function takes this answer as its input and answers NOTHING for what "includes" leaves open)
